# A parallel-plate electrostatic actuator. A voltage charges the plates through R;
# the moving plate hangs on a spring. One C-field holds the electrical and the
# mechanical energy, E = q1^2*(g0 - q2)/(2*eA) + k*q2^2/2: its port 1 is the charge
# and voltage, its port 2 the plate's deflection and force. Above the pull-in
# voltage sqrt(8*k*g0^3/(27*eA)) = 0.544 (try V0 = 0.6) the plate snaps shut.

junction circuit 1: V-, R+, Act.1+
junction plate 1: Act.2+, m+, b+

element V Se value=V0*Heaviside(t)
element R R R=R
element Act Cfield e1=q1*(g0-q2)/eA e2=k*q2-q1^2/(2*eA)
element m I I=m
element b R R=b

output x = q_Act_2
output i = f_R
output V_cap = e_Act

# --- editor data (comments; bondgraph.py ignores these) ---
#@title Electrostatic actuator (C-field, pull-in)
#@pos V 100 240
#@pos circuit 280 240
#@pos R 280 100
#@pos Act 480 240
#@pos plate 680 240
#@pos m 680 100
#@pos b 680 380
#@param V0=0.5
#@param R=0.1
#@param g0=1
#@param eA=1
#@param k=1
#@param m=1
#@param b=0.5
#@sim tEnd=30 steps=3000
